# Copy to .env to turn on live place search.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# With nothing set, the picker uses the built-in list of Lagos and Abuja
# landmarks and everything still works. Users can also always type a place
# name freehand, which is the real safety net whichever provider you pick.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTION 1 — OpenStreetMap via Photon.  Free. No key, no account, no billing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_PLACES_PROVIDER=photon
#
# Komoot run the public Photon instance free of charge for reasonable use.
# Unlike Nominatim — whose usage policy rules out type-ahead querying — Photon
# is built for autocomplete, so it is the OSM option that suits this screen.
# For production traffic, self-host it (it is open source) rather than leaning
# on the public instance.
#
# Coverage is the catch. Measured against Photon in Lagos:
#
#   "Chicken Republic"     found, Lagos and Ikeja
#   "Computer Village"     found, Ikeja
#   "NNPC Airport Road"    MISSED — returned a station in Delta State
#   "Oyingbo Market"       MISSED — returned a generic market in Ikorodu
#
# OSM knows roads, districts and chain brands. It is thin on individual
# filling stations and markets, which is much of what this app gets asked
# about. Judge whether that is acceptable before shipping it.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTION 2 — Google Places.  Best coverage. Needs an account and billing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=your-key-here
#
# Google Cloud console -> enable "Places API (New)" -> Credentials.
# Also enable "Geocoding API" on the same key if you want "use my current
# location" to resolve to a street name — reverse geocoding is a separate
# product from Places. Without it the app falls back to showing coordinates.
# A billing account is required. Google moved Places to per-SKU pricing with
# its own free tier in 2025, so check the current rates for the Autocomplete
# and Place Details SKUs before you ship.
#
# IMPORTANT: EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the JavaScript bundle at
# build time. This key ships to every client and anyone can read it. Restrict
# it in the Cloud console or it will be abused:
#
#   Web      Application restrictions -> HTTP referrers -> your domains
#   iOS      Application restrictions -> iOS apps -> your bundle identifier
#   Android  Application restrictions -> Android apps -> package + SHA-1
#   All      API restrictions -> Places API only, and set a daily quota cap
#
# If you would rather the key never reached the client, proxy the two fetches
# in utils/places.ts through your own backend and point them at it instead.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Other free tiers worth a look if neither fits: Geoapify, LocationIQ and
# Maptiler all wrap OSM data with a keyed free allowance and their own
# autocomplete endpoints. Mapbox Search sits between Photon and Google on both
# coverage and cost. All of them slot into the same two functions.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# EXPO_PUBLIC_PLACES_PROVIDER=photon
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=
